## Summary

Issue #165 (from gaylemcd) asked for the shared HCA mailbox, hca@heliosschool.org, to be able to sign in to the Heliosian sites and host events, to help with the newsletter and cafe invites.

What I found: to sign in, an address has to be a Google account in the heliosschool.org domain (`internal/auth/auth.go`) and also a `PERSON_EMAIL` row on an active, visible `PERSON` (`Model.SignedIn` in `internal/db/http.go`). No hca@ address existed, and no hand-added people exist at all. So it could have been done as data only: one hand-added "HCA" person with that address. That only works if hca@ is a real Google account and not a Google Group. Invite emails show the hosts' names as the sender and send replies to the hosts' addresses (`invitemail.go`), so an "HCA" host would have meant invites "From: HCA", with replies going to hca@.

Decision: ian chose not to build it. Board members already sign in as themselves and can write the newsletter and send invites. A role-account "person" would show up in Who? search, edits would be credited to "HCA" instead of whoever made them, and everyone using it would share one login. A code-level "role account" concept was also rejected as too much machinery. Issue #165 was closed as not planned with that explanation, and this branch only removes the item from TODO.md.

